a-controls="replo-:Ram32:" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-uuv62o"><div data-rid="135cf0cb-c56f-4582-b087-0e1c31207c36" class="r-sxhbsf"><div data-rid="110921ed-05c3-4129-aee0-551e9e5336e7" class="r-lpg43h" aria-hidden="true"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="currentColor" stroke-width="0" viewBox="0 0 16 16" role="img" aria-label="Collapse/Expand" style="width:var(--rsw, 100%);height:100%" class="r-1gtjen9" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M8 4a.5.5 0 0 1 .5.5v3h3a.5.5 0 0 1 0 1h-3v3a.5.5 0 0 1-1 0v-3h-3a.5.5 0 0 1 0-1h3v-3A.5.5 0 0 1 8 4"></path></svg></div></div><div data-rid="5f55e80e-6a2f-4289-a2f2-ab4fd642df8f" class="r-jqlrie alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Can it work without direct sunlight?</p></span></div></div><div class="replo-animated" hidden="" id="replo-:Ram32:"><div data-rid="57e9288f-b844-4522-b0b1-bcc7615d63ce" class="r-4xtzg4"><div data-rid="e7ee2a92-be6e-44f7-bd3d-2ba0bb7b2887" class="r-1lve9uw alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p> Yep! The CoolBreeze™ Solar Fan Hat charges via solar panels when you're in the sun, but it also comes with a USB charging port. That means you can pre-charge it the night before and still enjoy a full day of airflow even on cloudy days.</p></span></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="eaa4bf1c-6a9b-4752-87b8-5defd6b9ee41" class="r-5sk3ms" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-rid="8e67361b-28d4-4eed-ac68-1d1acb598395" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="replo-:Rem32:" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-x5kq2e"><div data-rid="797207a2-e2b6-4efb-8baf-548e9c67f1a2" class="r-c89rl4"><div data-rid="63fde7c7-6289-4679-8669-3ff3cc385ddd" class="r-1bz0k8v" aria-hidden="true"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="currentColor" stroke-width="0" viewBox="0 0 16 16" role="img" aria-label="Collapse/Expand" style="width:var(--rsw, 100%);height:100%" class="r-thbncs" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M8 4a.5.5 0 0 1 .5.5v3h3a.5.5 0 0 1 0 1h-3v3a.5.5 0 0 1-1 0v-3h-3a.5.5 0 0 1 0-1h3v-3A.5.5 0 0 1 8 4"></path></svg></div></div><div data-rid="14c6202a-6b8e-478b-9963-7fcf347e3b4c" class="r-lll8ef alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Is it waterproof?</p></span></div></div><div class="replo-animated" hidden="" id="replo-:Rem32:"><div data-rid="ad03e5cc-c1e0-4af9-aa74-3c19a68bf40f" class="r-bn7cdu"><div data-rid="7aa479ff-d627-4560-a1bc-928c42d83161" class="r-qf91te alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>The hat is made with water-resistant fabric, so it can handle light rain or splashes - perfect for fishing or gardening. Just avoid dunking it completely, as the electronics aren't built for a swim!</p></span></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="eabf9df2-d57e-47b1-b1ac-88e1618645d3" class="r-58m8oo" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-rid="c4e7893a-f7d8-4b94-8661-62a781f873d7" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="replo-:Rim32:" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-1n6rv27"><div data-rid="d81bd366-d573-41ba-b11d-f7b3dca55390" class="r-ejd4pl"><div data-rid="0e90f4f4-b9d7-45dd-a25d-7653a3daff63" class="r-9211t8" aria-hidden="true"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="currentColor" stroke-width="0" viewBox="0 0 16 16" role="img" aria-label="Collapse/Expand" style="width:var(--rsw, 100%);height:100%" class="r-18vumcm" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M8 4a.5.5 0 0 1 .5.5v3h3a.5.5 0 0 1 0 1h-3v3a.5.5 0 0 1-1 0v-3h-3a.5.5 0 0 1 0-1h3v-3A.5.5 0 0 1 8 4"></path></svg></div></div><div data-rid="8e5defe4-994a-422d-a586-4389ac539c7e" class="r-81at2f alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p> Does it really keep you cool?</p></span></div></div><div class="replo-animated" hidden="" id="replo-:Rim32:"><div data-rid="01aecc49-02c3-4a18-8d15-029f6fc0fd98" class="r-7xi2d2"><div data-rid="204b772f-e832-41b9-bec9-62155d6b87d2" class="r-e8k856 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Absolutely. The dual fans circulate fresh air around your face and scalp, cutting down sweat and heat buildup. Customers say it feels like a mini-breeze following them everywhere - ideal for camping, mowing, fishing, or working in the sun.</p></span></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="b1b709e8-5d71-4d3f-849a-3472c412da20" class="r-vvldk4" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-rid="3f0832d0-144e-413e-82e4-a5bb84349e03" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="replo-:Rmm32:" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-1b6owih"><div data-rid="d177f8fe-5ee9-4a3a-b85b-e14ba5a6f155" class="r-10ul3v"><div data-rid="62248be4-da2e-41fe-9348-e98c219cbbd0" class="r-qik5wv" aria-hidden="true"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="currentColor" stroke-width="0" viewBox="0 0 16 16" role="img" aria-label="Collapse/Expand" style="width:var(--rsw, 100%);height:100%" class="r-psdpam" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M8 4a.5.5 0 0 1 .5.5v3h3a.5.5 0 0 1 0 1h-3v3a.5.5 0 0 1-1 0v-3h-3a.5.5 0 0 1 0-1h3v-3A.5.5 0 0 1 8 4"></path></svg></div></div><div data-rid="cec67e91-60a4-4545-b748-ec68b733e5a7" class="r-1ftp1xu alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>What size heads does it fit?</p></span></div></div><div class="replo-animated" hidden="" id="replo-:Rmm32:"><div data-rid="894cc9be-c589-4272-b6c8-865780cb149e" class="r-15qrbdj"><div data-rid="9073729d-f882-4cae-8c5c-b4584eaf9ded" class="r-2esmy5 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>It's one-size-fits-all with an adjustable elastic drawstring, so it comfortably fits most adult head sizes (about 56 - 64 cm). It stays snug without squeezing.</p></span></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="06695e0b-014d-4a3d-a5fd-0a5cf44dd9bb" class="r-18w0ywq" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-rid="509c5010-0da8-47a4-bb67-b7a799b2a1a6" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="replo-:Rqm32:" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-1s1vc6b"><div data-rid="51f5fe0b-310b-4715-8ea5-8e5cdcac29f3" class="r-13j831s"><div data-rid="399fb328-8d9f-439d-b556-ed6f7e4094a9" class="r-1peq999" aria-hidden="true"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="currentColor" stroke-width="0" viewBox="0 0 16 16" role="img" aria-label="Collapse/Expand" style="width:var(--rsw, 100%);height:100%" class="r-o8weu3" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M8 4a.5.5 0 0 1 .5.5v3h3a.5.5 0 0 1 0 1h-3v3a.5.5 0 0 1-1 0v-3h-3a.5.5 0 0 1 0-1h3v-3A.5.5 0 0 1 8 4"></path></svg></div></div><div data-rid="8a3d4e8a-aa44-4862-976e-b8e2949e8682" class="r-8szg1p alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>How much sun protection does it give?</p></span></div></div><div class="replo-animated" hidden="" id="replo-:Rqm32:"><div data-rid="09a34047-92b5-4588-b5bd-0b1157087623" class="r-7mehu1"><div data-rid="cba82b3b-c75a-40dd-81b9-09cfe92d799a" class="r-bb9m4v alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>The wide brim provides UPF 50+ protection, blocking 98% of harmful UV rays. It shields your face, neck, and ears, keeping you safe even under harsh Aussie sun.</p></span></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="4631c2de-63d3-4481-ba89-43edb89f27a7" class="r-1qi8v39" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-rid="af2028fa-cc26-46e1-8650-38428f5396f6" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="replo-:Rum32:" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-1c8v4c5"><div data-rid="a5e1eb36-5ab0-484f-82d6-58bab3ec0777" class="r-3ueklx"><div data-rid="2aef5e5f-bb1b-4aed-b19d-7208349b3705" class="r-go16oa" aria-hidden="true"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="currentColor" stroke-width="0" viewBox="0 0 16 16" role="img" aria-label="Collapse/Expand" style="width:var(--rsw, 100%);height:100%" class="r-15wdzmy" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M8 4a.5.5 0 0 1 .5.5v3h3a.5.5 0 0 1 0 1h-3v3a.5.5 0 0 1-1 0v-3h-3a.5.5 0 0 1 0-1h3v-3A.5.5 0 0 1 8 4"></path></svg></div></div><div data-rid="875e8024-cb64-495e-a9ee-a370a5019494" class="r-15dktbk alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Is it heavy to wear?</p></span></div></div><div class="replo-animated" hidden="" id="replo-:Rum32:"><div data-rid="9b51e908-f867-4114-8ea5-772c3eb9ee68" class="r-aznast"><div data-rid="281e0c8c-2ffd-40cb-8d3a-7a7775bc7cd6" class="r-ng6fr7 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p> Not at all — it's lighter than a can of Coke. You'll barely notice it's there, even after hours outdoors. The fans are quiet, balanced, and don't make the hat top-heavy or bulky.</p></span></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="d53f0190-9da6-4249-a84f-a1229c2f5cd0" class="r-v3xpi" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-rid="7d61cbf6-dca8-488e-be13-44c841779123" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="replo-:R12m32:" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-sau3yr"><div data-rid="c661f6b9-1600-4508-985b-35caf26526d3" class="r-dxs7bd"><div data-rid="12356dcf-2fd0-4f7d-9e0f-edc321bb9cc0" class="r-m8dy1n" aria-hidden="true"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="currentColor" stroke-width="0" viewBox="0 0 16 16" role="img" aria-label="Collapse/Expand" style="width:var(--rsw, 100%);height:100%" class="r-gbllcr" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M8 4a.5.5 0 0 1 .5.5v3h3a.5.5 0 0 1 0 1h-3v3a.5.5 0 0 1-1 0v-3h-3a.5.5 0 0 1 0-1h3v-3A.5.5 0 0 1 8 4"></path></svg></div></div><div data-rid="809ac0d9-865a-4c06-b2b6-5d5f0f6105eb" class="r-nkf1no alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>How do you charge it?</p></span></div></div><div class="replo-animated" hidden="" id="replo-:R12m32:"><div data-rid="5a6b353d-48d9-412c-bc7b-594b5a5b7250" class="r-gqq9g4"><div data-rid="66c250e6-e06d-42f1-a470-e7fb054a38b6" class="r-irc5j5 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>You've got two options:</p><ul><li><p>﻿﻿Solar charging when outdoors *</p></li><li><p>﻿﻿USB charging at night or indoors O<br>The hat automatically switches to solar mode in sunlight and battery mode in shade -<br>no buttons or fuss.</p></li></ul></span></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div data-replo-marquee-root="true" data-rid="57edfbef-3c8c-4366-946a-1be8e880f57b" class="r-tnpya"><div class="r-a30uwj" data-replo-marquee-track="true"><div data-rid="cb7e23ae-0d1e-418c-933f-10e7cfaaace8" class="r-1xwvk4z"><picture data-rid="22257eba-8d6a-404b-a761-403ebefc6eca" class="r-aj83bf"><source srcSet="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/0f851ad3-0eca-4f80-8e2d-a34ae0165814/0f429a79-9467-4ccb-ab96-1f3a77212fa1?width=260" media="(max-width: 640px)"/><source srcSet="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/0f851ad3-0eca-4f80-8e2d-a34ae0165814/0f429a79-9467-4ccb-ab96-1f3a77212fa1?width=300" media="(min-width: 641px) and (max-width: 1024px)"/><source srcSet="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/0f851ad3-0eca-4f80-8e2d-a34ae0165814/0f429a79-9467-4ccb-ab96-1f3a77212fa1?width=300" media="(min-width: 1025px) and (max-width: 2400px)"/><img src="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/0f851ad3-0eca-4f80-8e2d-a34ae0165814/0f429a79-9467-4ccb-ab96-1f3a77212fa1" class="r-f9ixcc" loading="eager"/></picture><picture data-rid="7acdb487-691b-4964-b6fb-0e109facef06" class="r-mob1bk"><source srcSet="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/0f851ad3-0eca-4f80-8e2d-a34ae0165814/1e7ef33b-5f34-41e6-952f-2242f6255047?width=260" media="(max-width: 640px)"/><source srcSet="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/0f851ad3-0eca-4f80-8e2d-a34ae0165814/1e7ef33b-5f34-41e6-952f-2242f6255047?width=300" media="(min-width: 641px) and (max-width: 1024px)"/><source srcSet="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/0f851ad3-0eca-4f80-8e2d-a34ae0165814/1e7ef33b-5f34-41e6-952f-2242f6255047?width=300" media="(min-width: 1025px) and (max-width: 2400px)"/><img src="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/0f851ad3-0eca-4f80-8e2d-a34ae0165814/1e7ef33b-5f34-41e6-952f-2242f6255047" class="r-ng3u6k" loading="eager"/></picture><picture data-rid="3f6c9143-344b-4bff-9a68-fca57bc681a4" class="r-v8agqp"><source srcSet="https: